    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2956" root="بغم" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَبْغُومٌ</span></b>  A young gazelle, and a young camel,
<i>to which the cry termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُغَام</span> <i>is addressed by its
mother.</i> (JK.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  One says, also, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُغَامٌ مَبْغُومٌ</span> [<i>A
cry</i> &amp;c. <i>uttered</i>]; like as one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوْلٌ مَقُولٌ</span>.
(TA.)

